.TH SWAP.CONF 5 "SEPTEMBER 2026" "systemd-swap 0.2.0" swap.conf
.\" disable french spacing
.ss 12 0
.SH NAME
swap.conf \- systemd-swap configuration files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP /etc/systemd/swap.conf.d/*.conf
.IP /run/systemd/swap.conf.d/*.conf
.IP /usr/lib/systemd/swap.conf.d/*.conf
.IP /etc/systemd/swap.conf
.IP /usr/share/systemd-swap/swap-default.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
These configuration files control the zram pool, zswap and the dynamic swap files managed by
.BR systemd-swap (8).
.SH CONFIGURATION DIRECTORIES AND PRECEDENCE
.PP
The default configuration is defined during compilation, so a configuration file is only needed when it is necessary to deviate from those defaults.
By default, the configuration file in /etc/systemd/ contains commented out entries showing the defaults as a guide to the administrator.
This file can be edited to create local overrides.
.PP
When packages need to customize the configuration, they can install configuration snippets in /usr/lib/systemd/swap.conf.d/.
The main configuration file is read before any of the configuration directories, and has the lowest precedence; entries in a file in any configuration directory override entries in the single configuration file.
Files in the swap.conf.d/ configuration subdirectories are sorted by their filename in lexicographic order, regardless of in which of the subdirectories they reside.
When multiple files specify the same option, for options which accept just a single value, the entry in the file with the lexicographically latest name takes precedence.
.PP
Files in /etc/ are reserved for the local administrator, who may use this logic to override the configuration files installed by vendor packages.
It is recommended to prefix all filenames in those subdirectories with a two-digit number and a dash, to simplify the ordering of the files.
.PP
To disable a configuration file supplied by the vendor, the recommended way is to place a symlink to /dev/null in the configuration directory in /etc/, with the same filename as the vendor configuration file.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
Sizes accept the suffixes K, M, G and T, or a percentage of RAM where noted.
In auto mode the daemon injects the values marked "auto" in
/usr/share/systemd-swap/swap-default.conf; any value set in a configuration
file takes precedence.
.SS Mode
.IP swap_mode=
.B auto
(default) picks zram with swap files when the swap file system is btrfs, ext4
or xfs with at least as much free space as RAM, and zram alone otherwise
(live systems included).
.B zram+swapfile
uses a zram pool as primary swap and swap files for overflow.
.B zswap+swapfile
uses zswap in front of swap files.
.B zram
uses the zram pool only.
.B manual
enables only the subsystems switched on by
.BR zram_enabled= ,
.B zswap_enabled=
and
.BR swapfile_enabled= .
.B disabled
leaves swap alone and exits.
.IP "zram_enabled=, zswap_enabled=, swapfile_enabled="
Manual mode only. yes/y/1/true enables the subsystem; anything else leaves it off.
.SS Zram pool
.IP zram_size=
Upper bound on the total disksize of the pool, as a size or a percentage of RAM
(default 150%, at least 50%). The pool starts with one device at 95% of
.B zram_mem_limit
and grows toward this bound only by the RAM compression has saved.
.IP zram_mem_limit=
Ceiling on the RAM the pool may hold, as a size or a percentage of RAM
(default 50%). 0 removes it; the pool is then sized from
.B zram_size
directly and can exhaust RAM on incompressible data.
.IP zram_alg=
Compression algorithm (default zstd): any listed in
/sys/block/zram*/comp_algorithm, such as lz4 or lzo.
.IP zram_prio=
Swap priority of the first device (default 32767). Each added device gets the next lower one.
.IP zram_max_devices=
Most devices the pool may grow to, 1\(en8 (default 8).
.IP zram_expand_threshold=
Expand when the pool is fuller than this percentage, 50\(en95 (default 85).
.IP zram_contract_threshold=
Contract when the pool stays under this percentage, 5\(en50 (default 20).
.IP zram_expand_cooldown=
Seconds between expansions, 5\(en120 (default 10).
.IP zram_contract_stability=
Seconds the pool must stay under the contract threshold before a device is
removed, 30\(en600 (default 120).
.IP zram_check_interval=
Longest wait between checks in seconds, 3\(en300 (default 5). Memory pressure (PSI) wakes the monitor at once.
.SS Zram writeback
.PP
Pages nobody has read for a while are written to a sparse file behind a loop
device, one per zram device, and their RAM is returned. Needs a kernel with
CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK and CONFIG_ZRAM_TRACK_ENTRY_ACTIME.
.IP zram_writeback_size=
Disk budget for the whole pool, as a size or a percentage of RAM (default 50%).
0 turns writeback off.
.IP zram_writeback_path=
Directory for the backing files (default: swapfile_path). It must stay inside
the service unit's ReadWritePaths=.
.IP zram_writeback_threshold=
Only write back while the pool holds more than this percentage of
.B zram_mem_limit
(default 20).
.IP zram_writeback_idle=
Seconds a page must go untouched to qualify (default 3600).
.IP zram_writeback_interval=
Seconds between passes (default 300).
.SS Zswap
.IP zswap_compressor=
Compression algorithm (default zstd).
.IP zswap_zpool=
Compressed memory allocator (default zsmalloc).
.IP zswap_max_pool_percent=
Largest share of RAM the compressed pool may use (default 45).
.IP zswap_shrinker_enabled=
1 moves cold pages to disk when the pool is full (default 1).
.IP zswap_accept_threshold=
Resume accepting pages when the pool drops to this percentage (default 80).
.SS Swap files
.PP
Preallocated files (NOCOW on btrfs) created under memory pressure and removed
when idle. Their priority is below zram, so the kernel uses them once zram is
full.
.IP swapfile_path=
Directory for the swap files (default /swapfile).
.IP swapfile_chunk_size=
Size of each file (default 512M).
.IP swapfile_max_count=
Most files at once, capped at 28 (default 28).
.IP swapfile_min_count=
Files kept even when swap is idle (default 1).
.IP swapfile_free_ram_perc=
No file is removed while free RAM is under this percentage (default 20). A file is created at once, whatever this says, when free RAM is under 10% and total free swap is under two chunks.
.IP swapfile_free_swap_perc=
Create a file when the files' free space falls under this percentage (default 40).
.IP swapfile_remove_free_swap_perc=
Remove a file when the files' free space is above this percentage (default 70).
.IP swapfile_frequency=
Seconds between checks while files exist, 1\(en86400 (default 1).
.IP swapfile_shrink_threshold=
A file less used than this percentage may be removed, 10\(en50 (default 30).
.IP swapfile_safe_headroom=
Percentage the remaining files must keep free after absorbing a removed file's
pages, 20\(en60 (default 40).
.SS MGLRU
.IP mglru_min_ttl_ms=
Pages younger than this many milliseconds are not reclaimed (default 1000;
0 leaves the kernel setting alone). Needs a kernel with MGLRU.
.SH AUTHOR
Vilgot Fredenberg <vilgot@fredenberg.xyz>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR systemd-swap (8)
